Operator authorized saved-state reset, UI kill and restart.
Backed up exact window/state and window/epoch bytes privately, invalidated
old epoch and cleared persisted UI state, killed only the UI we started,
then launched the UI in a detached process session. Restored the swarm cwd
from that backup. The supervisor and harnesses stayed alive; the actual
Codex TUI PID/generation remained unchanged through logic replacement.
Backup: ~/Library/Logs/bboxy450-term/window-reset-20261027-165435/.

Mechanisms:
- proto gui::MAX_REPLY_BYTES: 64 MiB bounded GUI reply budget.
- mux read_gui_line/send: GUI snapshots use that budget; seat send/read and
  GUI requests keep the existing 1 MiB bound.
- cockpit read_replies and ctl Client::reply use the same GUI budget.
- control-service version 2 replaces older logic while retaining PTYs.
- startup retries a missing GUI endpoint through one confirmed owner refresh;
  failed shutdown of an already departed process does not abort that refresh.
- swarm row says cwd; no change to launch folder semantics.
- real MCP spawn/split boundary is explicitly selected in Make/night, per #327 B2.

